<title>USA: Grubb &amp; Ellis declines comment on share rise.</title>
<headline>Grubb &amp; Ellis declines comment on share rise.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Grubb &amp; Ellis Co said that, in keeping with company policy, it had no comment on its stock's unusual market activity today, according to the New York Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>The company's shares rose one to 6-3/8.</p>
<p>The NYSE said it had contacted the company and requested the company issue a public statement indicating whether any corporate developments could explain the shares' activity.</p>
</text>
